From b8095897fc4499570490342a9e5625135cdb20a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 02:31:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/18] klzh2: tANS for the code streams, finer match-length
 codes, coded low offset bits

The token and length-code streams are coded with an original tabled ANS coder (two states
over one bit stream, bit-reversal spread, tables of up to 2^11 states with a compact count
header) in place of khuf chunks; literals stay on khuf blocks. Match lengths get 48 direct
codes and two per octave after (nci: the bulk of the gap to zstd was here), and the low four
bits of new offsets become a coded stream when their histogram says so (binary and sample
data: mozilla, x-ray, osdb). Measured basis in results/R01-work/exp-streams-level*.txt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FUEN4aRWhUw7yL7cZMqTmZ
---
